BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(MADURAI BENCH\)
CASE NO: W.P.\(MD\) No. 8190 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: HCMD010912342026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice M.S. Ramesh & Justice M. Nirmal Kumar

PARTIES:
Rameswaram Traditional Fishermen Welfare Association
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
Union of India, Ministry of External Affairs & Government of Tamil Nadu, Fisheries Department
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Constitution of India, Territorial Waters, Continental Shelf, Exclusive Economic Zone and other Maritime Zones Act 1976

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
Article 21, Maritime Zones Act Section 6

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Traditional Fishing Rights, Palk Strait, Maritime Boundary, Livelihood Protection, Diplomatic Retrieval

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Artisanal fishermen from Rameswaram had 68 mechanized trawlers impounded across International Maritime Boundary Line.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Does continuous deprivation of means of maritime livelihood trigger State's constitutional obligation to protect citizens abroad?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Right to livelihood under Article 21 imposes affirmative obligation on the Union to protect citizens' occupational survival through diplomatic channels.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Writ Petition Allowed; Central Government directed to expedite diplomatic retrieval of seized mechanized fishing trawlers.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice M.S. Ramesh & Justice M. Nirmal Kumar
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
